            }
          ]
        },
        "IMAGING": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "IMAGING",
          "canonical_heading": "IMAGING",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Abdominal radiography—evaluate constipation or obstipation, prostatomegaly, sublumbar lymphadenomegaly, location of urinary bladder and prostate, and megacolon in cats.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Pelvic radiography—evaluate pelvic fracture malunion, intrapelvic mass, caudal displacement of the prostate and bladder, entrapment of bladder or bowel in hernia.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Abdominal ultrasonography—evaluate the size and consistency of the prostate, location of urinary bladder and prostate, intrapelvic or caudal abdominal masses, sublumbar lymphadenomegaly, presence of abdominal cryptorchid testicle.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Perineal ultrasonography—evaluate presence of abdominal viscera or masses.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
        "DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURES": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURES",
          "canonical_heading": "DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURES",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Visual perianal examination:",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Normally the anus and EAS are held in",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "position dorsal and slightly cranial to the caudal extent of the tuber ischii.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "When the perineal diaphragm is",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "weakened, the anus migrates caudally. May be severe in bilateral PH.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Eliciting a cough reflex by gentle tracheal",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "palpation will increase intra-abdominal pressure and aid evaluation of the position and movement of the anus.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Rectal examination:",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Confirm accumulation of feces in the dilated",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "and sacculated rectum and perineal laxity.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "If the integrity of the pelvic diaphragm",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "has been compromised, it will be possible to pinch the rectal mucosa and skin together between the tip of the forefinger and thumb without palpating a muscle shelf in between.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Evaluate both sides; bilateral PH is",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "common especially in intact male dogs.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Endoscopy or percutaneous fine-needle aspiration biopsy may be indicated if a mass lesion is present extra- or intraluminally.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        },
