        "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS": {
          "present": true,
          "status": "content",
          "source_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "canonical_heading": "SURGICAL CONSIDERATIONS",
          "content_blocks": [
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Castration of male dogs should always be performed simultaneously with herniorrhaphy, due to the high rate of recurrence in intact dogs regardless of surgical technique used.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "In patients with bladder retroflexion and entrapment, the urethra should be catheterized, and the bladder decompressed if possible:",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Percutaneous perineal cystocentesis may",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "be required to decompress and reposition the bladder before a urethral catheter can be passed.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "If the bladder is able to be decompressed,",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "correction of biochemical abnormalities is preferred prior to anesthesia and surgery in the urinary obstruction patient with PH.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Prior to surgical correction, the author prefers the use of an epidural with local anesthetic and/or morphine.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Impacted feces should be gently removed from the rectum prior to surgery:",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Enemas are not recommended as liquid",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "feces may not be completely evacuated, leading to excessive contamination during surgery and postoperatively.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Primary repair of the weakened muscles alone often leads to recurrence and is not recommended as the only form of repair.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "The internal obturator muscle flap is the preferred local method of repair combined with primary bolstering of the perineal musculature. The author prefers to repair both sides of the pelvic diaphragm regardless of the unilateral nature of the hernia.",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "It may be helpful in large dogs with large bilateral hernias, especially if bladder",
              "pdf_page": 1143,
              "printed_page": 1061,
              "column": 3
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "retroflexion or visceral entrapment, to perform exploratory laparotomy, reposition the bladder and rectum, and perform incisional colopexy and cystopexy:",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Herniorrhaphy can be performed at a",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "later time (2–7 days), when the patient’s condition has stabilized and the perineal edema has resolved.",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "In patients with poor perineal muscle",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "development and in patients with large defects, the repair is often bolstered with the use of secondary local muscle flaps.",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "Absorbable and nonabsorbable mesh",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "implants are needed in some severe cases.",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 1,
              "text": "A superficial gluteal muscle flap is",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "recommended in cats and very small dogs to bolster the internal obturator muscle flap and primary repair techniques.",
              "pdf_page": 1144,
              "printed_page": 1062,
              "column": 1
            }
          ]
        },
